<title>BRAZIL: No sign of TCK in Argentine wheat held in Brazil.</title>
<headline>No sign of TCK in Argentine wheat held in Brazil.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A cargo of Argentine wheat held up in the Brazilian river port of Corumba does not contain any sign of tilletia controversa kuhn or TCK fungus, a Brazilian Agriculture Ministry official said.</p>
<p>The cargo of just over 5,000 tonnes has been held for over a month pending the results of tests after a claim it may originally be of German origin and part of a cargo which was refused entry into Brazil last year because of alleged TCK contamination.</p>
<p>However the results of a sample were sent to authorities on Monday which showed no evidence of TCK and so the wheat is now being released, the official said.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
